I walk out into the hallway.
My new plant stands on the floor.
It is a small, green plant.
I take the plant.
I carry it into the living room.
There is a large window in the living room.
I put the plant on the windowsill.
I take a step back.
Now the plant stands in the window.
The winter sun is shining.
The plant stands perfectly in the pale light.
I go out into the kitchen.
There is a small watering can standing under the sink.
I take the watering can.
I water my new plant.
There are two dead leaves lying by the flowerpot.
I remove the leaves.
I throw them in the trash can.
I put the watering can on the floor by the window.
The sun shines on the wet, green leaves.
